    "summary": "Incendiary Eleven > Caution suite and soaring Dark Star",
    "blurb": "Features a blazing Eleven > Caution sequence and an expansive Dark Star. Jerry’s inventive guitar shines throughout, while the set closes with the gentle “And We Bid You Good Night.” The soundboard capture is well‑balanced for ’69, offering solid instrument separation despite typical mud.",
    "review": "The February 5, 1969 show at Soldiers' and Sailors' Memorial Hall captures the Dead in a high‑energy stride. From the gritty opener of “Turn On Your Lovelight” through a fluid middle that weaves Dark Star into Saint Stephen, the band builds momentum into an incendiary Eleven > Caution suite where Jerry’s scorching guitar work is nothing short of “tremendous.” The set then eases into a tranquil close with “And We Bid You Good Night,” providing a balanced arc of intensity and calm. Listeners benefit from a well‑balanced soundboard tape that, while bearing the era's characteristic mud, delivers clear instrument separation and preserves the fire‑filled spirit of this early ’70s transition period.",
